# aeogeosearch.com — Netlify _redirects
# Put this file in your PUBLISH directory (usually dist/ or public/).
# prerender.mjs copies it there automatically.
#
# IMPORTANT: delete any existing catch-all SPA rewrite such as
#     /*    /index.html    200
# from netlify.toml, _redirects, or the Netlify UI. That rule makes EVERY junk
# URL (/$ , /* , /admin/ , /month , /nonsense-page-xyz) return HTTP 200 with
# your homepage — Google calls these "soft 404s".
#
# Netlify notes that shaped this file:
#   * Rules are first-match-wins, top to bottom.
#   * A rule does NOT shadow an existing file unless it ends with "!" (force).
#   * Trailing slashes are normalised BEFORE rules run, so you must NOT write
#     "/about/ -> /about" rules — they cause redirect loops. Pretty URLs
#     (on by default) already standardises slashless URLs.
#   * Query parameters are passed through on 301s, so a rule like
#     "/resources q=:q /resources 301" would loop. We deliberately do NOT
#     add it; the SearchAction markup is removed instead and /resources?q=...
#     resolves to a page whose canonical is /resources.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. Alias routes: one page, one URL (301, not canonical) -----------------
# These four pairs currently render identical React components. Google found
# the short versions as path-like strings inside your inline JS bundle.
# (Trailing-slash variants are listed too; Netlify normalises them first.)
/terms                 /terms-of-service      301
/terms/                /terms-of-service      301
/privacy               /privacy-policy        301
/privacy/              /privacy-policy        301
/aeo-geo-tools         /tools                 301
/aeo-geo-tools/        /tools                 301
/knowledge-library     /learn                 301
/knowledge-library/    /learn                 301

# --- 2. Normalise the homepage ------------------------------------------------
# "!" is required because /index.html is a real deployed file; without force,
# Netlify would serve the file instead of redirecting.
/index.html            /                      301!

# --- 3. Serve the pre-rendered HTML for each REAL route (200 = rewrite) ------
# These are internal rewrites: the browser URL stays /about. No catch-all.
/about                 /about.html            200
/services              /services.html         200
/pricing               /pricing.html          200
/what-is-aeom          /what-is-aeom.html     200
/resources             /resources.html        200
/learn                 /learn.html            200
/tools                 /tools.html            200
/visibility-tool       /visibility-tool.html  200
/terms-of-service      /terms-of-service.html 200
/privacy-policy        /privacy-policy.html   200
/accessibility         /accessibility.html    200
/contact               /contact.html          200

# The /assets/ folder (shared app.js + site.css) and /images/ are REAL files.
# Netlify shadowing means a non-forced splat rule like the one below never
# overrides an existing file, so those assets are served normally.
# --- 4. Safety net: a REAL 404 for anything not listed above ------------------
# A 404.html file alone is normally enough, but this explicit LAST rule also
# overrides any leftover "/*  /index.html  200" catch-all that might still be
# configured in netlify.toml (file-based _redirects rules run first).
# Shadowing means existing static files (robots.txt, sitemap.xml, images) still
# win, so this only fires for paths that don't exist — exactly /$ , /* , /& ,
# /month , /admin/ , /auth/ , /cart/ , /checkout/ , /account/ , /private/ ...
# which is what gets them permanently removed from Google's index.

